                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1a33e78e-5504-3166-9d95-d459b185aebb",
                        "entry_id": "c681cb0d-095c-3ff4-8715-ed93779661f7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To officiate at a funeral service for, to hold a funeral service for."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e73d4c66-f2cb-4efb-a55b-e9bf6b00f18d",
                                "sense_id": "1a33e78e-5504-3166-9d95-d459b185aebb",
                                "text": "Pardon me, for yielding to a temporary impulse of this character, at the hazard of seeming to funeralize, rather than compliment my congregation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "51bfd000-465d-4b61-9df7-0734500e9697",
                                "sense_id": "1a33e78e-5504-3166-9d95-d459b185aebb",
                                "text": "A gentleman who knew him, speaking of him to an American traveller a few years since, said — \"Sir he funeralized every congregation he took charge of.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0a93007b-c0a8-4a00-b75a-f8389d0b79e2",
                                "sense_id": "1a33e78e-5504-3166-9d95-d459b185aebb",
                                "text": "\"Old Uncle Sambo make a powerful prayer when they funeralized the body.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ab60fa9d-05ed-4fe9-8251-607e88b0d419",
                                "sense_id": "1a33e78e-5504-3166-9d95-d459b185aebb",
                                "text": "With Weaver gone this way he could not even be funeralized like a regular somebody. Big Young had been funeralized the properest that Eenie had ever seen, with a fine motor hearse of light purple color, and coffin-bearers with pure."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "026746af-05f1-4768-8b16-51352a446be4",
                                "sense_id": "1a33e78e-5504-3166-9d95-d459b185aebb",
                                "text": "[...] the preacher-man was weepy- eyed when he funeralized the corpse; [...]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7a437cb3-53c9-4386-9d83-1373e825463a",
                                "sense_id": "1a33e78e-5504-3166-9d95-d459b185aebb",
                                "text": "\"Two of them were funeralized down there in Robbins, Georgia. I reckon they got them all.\" \"Funeralized?\" \"That's right,\" he said in his soft voice. \"They never should have fooled around with that crowd.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
